噢，我的天。

615
00:24:32.030 --> 00:24:37.650
And then later you realize that no one is paid for, that everyone now, their bill is
后来你才发现，没人付钱，现在每个人的账单

616
00:24:37.650 --> 00:24:38.310
going to be double.
都要翻倍了。

617
00:24:38.470 --> 00:24:38.650
Double.
翻倍。

618
00:24:39.010 --> 00:24:39.650
Because they brought a plus one.
因为他们带了家属。

619
00:24:39.650 --> 00:24:41.410
And they wouldn't have probably even brought anyone.
而他们本来可能根本不会带任何人。

620
00:24:41.770 --> 00:24:45.150
So now, guys, we are going to move to the Chili's.
所以现在，伙计们，我们要去Chili's餐厅了。

621
00:24:45.270 --> 00:24:45.830
Oh, here we go.
噢，开始了。

622
00:24:45.830 --> 00:24:47.010
It's time to go to Chili's.
是时候去Chili's了。

623
00:24:47.050 --> 00:24:47.100
Here we go.
开始了。

624
00:24:47.210 --> 00:24:51.430
And if we look like we're sweating, it's because it was over 100 degrees when we shot this episode.
如果我们看起来在流汗，那是因为拍摄这一集时气温超过了100华氏度。

625
00:24:51.430 --> 00:24:55.450
And there was very little air conditioning inside this abandoned restaurant.
而且这家废弃餐厅里的空调几乎没用。

626
00:24:55.730 --> 00:25:00.050
I'm absolutely fine because when I'm completely comfortable, everyone is miserable.
我完全没问题，因为只要我感觉完全舒适，其他人就得遭殃。

627
00:25:00.390 --> 00:25:03.390
So I was doing okay as well.
所以我当时也还好。

628
00:25:03.570 --> 00:25:08.190
But the gentlemen, the men wearing suits were in a tuxedo.
但男士们，那些穿西装的男士们穿着燕尾服。

629
00:25:08.490 --> 00:25:10.710
And then he would put things on top of the tuxedo.
而且他还会往燕尾服外面套东西。

630
00:25:10.830 --> 00:25:11.030
Yeah.
是啊。

631
00:25:11.550 --> 00:25:11.990
Yeah.
是啊。

632
00:25:12.150 --> 00:25:14.510
We spent three full days filming there.
我们在那里整整拍了三天。

633
00:25:14.510 --> 00:25:19.970
And we also had to sometimes wear coats because we were pretending like it was fall.
而且我们有时还得穿外套，因为我们要假装那是秋天。

634
00:25:20.350 --> 00:25:22.930
If you see rain, he's got that big trench coat on.
如果你看到下雨，他身上就穿着那件大风衣。

635
00:25:23.190 --> 00:25:24.610
It always worked out that way.
总是这样安排。

636
00:25:24.690 --> 00:25:28.510
We would film all these episodes that we'll talk about where we were in coats and suits
我们会拍摄所有这些我们要谈论的剧集，我们在户外穿着外套和西装

637
00:25:28.510 --> 00:25:30.490
and stuff outside and it was AuguSt.
之类的，而当时其实是八月。

638
00:25:30.930 --> 00:25:36.510
Or we would have to pretend like it was spring, but we were shooting it during the winter and
或者我们得假装是春天，但我们是在冬天拍摄的，

639
00:25:36.510 --> 00:25:37.290
we would be freezing.
我们当时都快冻僵了。

640
00:25:37.550 --> 00:25:37.850
Yes.
是的。

641
00:25:38.510 --> 00:25:43.450
We never shot the episodes during the time of year in which they were.
我们从来没有在剧集设定的那个季节拍摄过。

642
00:25:43.630 --> 00:25:49.090
I love Oscar's talking head, his description of the Dundies, comparing them to a children's
我喜欢奥斯卡的采访片段，他对比邓迪奖和儿童

643
00:25:49.090 --> 00:25:49.390
party.
派对的描述。

644
00:25:49.530 --> 00:25:51.530
He did that so well.
他演得太好了。

645
00:25:51.710 --> 00:25:53.290
It was so spot on.
简直一针见血。

646
00:25:53.430 --> 00:25:55.550
Oscar always has some of my favorite talking heads.
奥斯卡总有一些我最喜欢的采访片段。

647
00:25:55.710 --> 00:25:56.350
He's brilliant.
他太有才了。

648
00:25:56.350 --> 00:25:57.650
He's an amazing actor.
他是一位了不起的演员。

649
00:25:57.890 --> 00:25:58.510
He really is.
确实如此。

650
00:25:58.590 --> 00:26:03.470
Oscar describes the Dundies as a child's birthday party and Pam compares it to an accident
奥斯卡把邓迪奖形容为儿童生日派对，而帕姆则把它比作一场事故。

651
00:26:03.470 --> 00:26:05.650
that you're forced to look at.
是你被迫去看的。

652
00:26:05.650 --> 00:26:06.610
You're forced to look at.
你被迫去看的。

653
00:26:06.610 --> 00:26:08.470
I have a question for you, Jenna.
我有个问题想问你，珍娜。

654
00:26:08.650 --> 00:26:08.830
Yeah.
没错。

655
00:26:09.170 --> 00:26:09.470
All right.
好吧。

656
00:26:09.610 --> 00:26:15.430
I read, when I was looking back over the Dundies, I read an article that said that BJ
我在回顾《邓迪奖》那集时读到一篇文章，说BJ

657
00:26:15.430 --> 00:26:21.070
Novak took Jenna out to get drunk in real life and then let her know what her responses
·诺瓦克在现实生活中带珍娜出去喝酒，然后让她知道自己的反应

658
00:26:21.070 --> 00:26:23.250
were like because you don't really drink that much in real life.
是什么样的，因为你在现实生活中其实并不怎么喝酒。

659
00:26:23.330 --> 00:26:24.990
So he took you out drinking.
所以他带你出去喝酒了。

660
00:26:24.990 --> 00:26:26.010
Is that true?
是真的吗？

661
00:26:26.250 --> 00:26:26.710
Yes.
是的。

662
00:26:27.190 --> 00:26:27.610
What?
什么？

663
00:26:27.910 --> 00:26:28.390
Yes.
是的。

664
00:26:28.430 --> 00:26:32.390
I was nervous about this episode because Pam had to be drunk.
我对这一集感到很紧张，因为帕姆必须表现出醉酒的状态。

665
00:26:32.590 --> 00:26:34.570
And that's hard to play and not be goofy.
要演好醉酒而不显得滑稽是很难的。

666
00:26:34.570 --> 00:26:35.210
It is.
确实如此。

667
00:26:35.290 --> 00:26:39.930
And I confided in the writers and I said, I'm nervous.
我向编剧们吐露了心声，我说，我很紧张。

668
00:26:40.230 --> 00:26:41.970
I don't know how to do it.
我不知道该怎么演。

669
00:26:42.130 --> 00:26:49.550
And Mindy had a great stage direction later where she was saying, you know, Pam is nodding
后来敏迪给了一个很棒的舞台指导，她说，你知道，帕姆在点头

670
00:26:49.550 --> 00:26:50.190
along.
表示赞同。

671
00:26:50.290 --> 00:26:51.130
I loved that.
我很喜欢那个。

672
00:26:51.390 --> 00:26:51.510
Nodding.
点头。

673
00:26:51.610 --> 00:26:55.810
That was in the script that Pam is nodding when she's really drunk.
剧本里写着帕姆在喝醉时会点头。

674
00:26:55.970 --> 00:26:56.910
That you're trying so hard to pay attention.
就是那种你非常努力地想要集中注意力的样子。

675
00:26:57.110 --> 00:26:57.350
Yes.
没错。

676
00:26:57.450 --> 00:26:57.950
Yeah, exactly.
对，就是这样。

677
00:26:57.950 --> 00:26:59.570
I'm a normal person paying attention.
我是一个正在集中注意力的正常人。

678
00:26:59.630 --> 00:26:59.850
Yes.
是的。

679
00:26:59.910 --> 00:27:01.010
Look how I'm nodding at you.
你看我怎么对你点头的。

680
00:27:01.010 --> 00:27:03.210
So that was Mindy's stage direction.
所以那是敏迪的舞台指导。

681
00:27:03.410 --> 00:27:07.110
But the rest of it, like, how do you gradually become drunk?
但剩下的部分，比如，你怎么逐渐变得醉醺醺的？

682
00:27:07.110 --> 00:27:12.510
And I was really afraid that I was going to do just some horrible, fake, drunky performance.
我真的很担心自己会演出一场糟糕、虚假、醉酒的戏。

683
00:27:12.810 --> 00:27:13.770
You did fantastic.
你演得太棒了。

684
00:27:14.130 --> 00:27:14.710
Thank you.
谢谢。

685
00:27:14.950 --> 00:27:20.990
So BJ and I get to talking and we decide, how about we go out, I'll have some drinks,
所以我和BJ聊了聊，我们决定，不如我们出去，我喝点酒，

686
00:27:21.210 --> 00:27:26.990
and BJ will ask me questions and help me observe what it feels like to slowly get drunk.
BJ问我问题，帮我观察慢慢变醉是什么感觉。

687
00:27:26.990 --> 00:27:29.810
So he was sort of going to document you having drinks.
所以他算是要记录你喝酒的过程。

688
00:27:30.030 --> 00:27:30.170
Yes.
是的。

689
00:27:30.290 --> 00:27:31.330
This is really method.
这真是体验派演法。

690
00:27:31.590 --> 00:27:32.090
This is super nerdy.
这太书呆子气了。

691
00:27:32.590 --> 00:27:33.590
I like it, though.
不过我喜欢。

692
00:27:33.730 --> 00:27:37.430
And I know why I didn't take you out, because I would have been the one also being like,
我知道为什么我没带你出去，因为我也会变成那个样子，说：

693
00:27:37.490 --> 00:27:38.230
I'll have drinks, too.
我也要喝酒。

694
00:27:38.350 --> 00:27:40.050
It's like, no, this defeats the purpose.
那样的话，这就不起作用了。

695
00:27:40.050 --> 00:27:41.530
This is a scientific experiment.
这是一项科学实验。

696
00:27:41.790 --> 00:27:41.870
Yeah.
没错。

697
00:27:42.310 --> 00:27:42.990
So, yeah.
所以，是的。

698
00:27:43.150 --> 00:27:44.410
So I went out with BJ.
所以我跟BJ出去了。

699
00:27:44.710 --> 00:27:50.210
And it was really interesting because after the first two drinks, I was like, oh, I just
这真的很有趣，因为喝完前两杯酒后，我就觉得，哦，我只是

700
00:27:50.210 --> 00:27:52.230
feel buzzed and a little dizzy.
感到微醺和一点点眩晕。

701
00:27:52.230 --> 00:27:58.070
I was laughing a lot, so that's why I had Pam do all of those ridiculous laughs in the
我当时笑得特别厉害，所以才让帕姆在那一集里

702
00:27:58.070 --> 00:27:58.490
episode.
发出了那么多滑稽的笑声。

703
00:27:58.710 --> 00:28:00.490
But by drink number four, I—
但喝到第四杯的时候，我——

704
00:28:00.490 --> 00:28:01.110
Four?
四杯？

705
00:28:01.390 --> 00:28:02.170
Number four?
第四杯？

706
00:28:02.290 --> 00:28:04.230
By drink number four, I was drinking Cosmopolitans.
喝到第四杯的时候，我喝的是大都会鸡尾酒。

707
00:28:04.830 --> 00:28:05.710
Oh, my gosh, Jenna.
天哪，珍娜。

708
00:28:05.830 --> 00:28:06.730
Did you get sick?
你喝吐了吗？

709
00:28:06.910 --> 00:28:08.210
I didn't get sick.
我没喝吐。

710
00:28:08.210 --> 00:28:09.190
Oh, good Lord.
天呐，我的老天。

711
00:28:09.350 --> 00:28:09.550
Okay.
好吧。

712
00:28:09.770 --> 00:28:09.870
I know.
我知道。

713
00:28:10.050 --> 00:28:15.130
So by drink number four, apparently I said to BJ, I don't feel drunk at all.
所以喝到第四杯时，我竟然跟BJ说，我一点都没觉得醉。

714
00:28:15.170 --> 00:28:15.770
I feel normal.
我觉得很正常。

715
00:28:16.650 --> 00:28:18.730
And BJ said, really?
BJ说，真的吗？

716
00:28:19.470 --> 00:28:23.730
Because you're talking really loud and really close, and you almost just fell over.
因为你说话声音特别大，离人特别近，而且刚才差点摔倒。

717
00:28:24.110 --> 00:28:25.510
And I was like, I did?
我说，我有吗？

718
00:28:26.630 --> 00:28:28.710
So I stopped after drink number four.
所以我喝完第四杯就停了。

719
00:28:28.850 --> 00:28:34.770
But I thought that it was really interesting how after so many drinks, I doubted that I
但我当时觉得挺有意思的，喝了那么多酒，我竟然怀疑自己

720
00:28:34.770 --> 00:28:35.630
was even drunk.
到底有没有醉。

721
00:28:36.150 --> 00:28:36.510
Yes.
没错。

722
00:28:36.730 --> 00:28:41.150
And so all that information, I kind of weaved into my performance.
所以我把这些信息都融入到了我的表演里。

723
00:28:41.590 --> 00:28:43.110
Well, it worked, lady.
好吧，效果很棒，女士。

724
00:28:43.350 --> 00:28:43.850
Thank you.
谢谢。

725
00:28:43.870 --> 00:28:45.410
And I'm glad you didn't have a hangover.
很高兴你没宿醉。

726
00:28:46.430 --> 00:28:48.330
So, folks, drink responsibly.
所以，各位，请理性饮酒。

727
00:28:48.570 --> 00:28:48.870
Yeah.
没错。

728
00:28:49.190 --> 00:28:50.530
Don't drink four, Cosmos.
别喝四杯大都会鸡尾酒。

729
00:28:50.850 --> 00:28:51.070
Yeah.
没错。

730
00:28:51.330 --> 00:28:52.610
Don't drink four, Cosmos.
别喝四杯大都会鸡尾酒。

731
00:28:52.610 --> 00:28:53.750
We do not recommend.
我们不推荐这样做。

732
00:28:54.910 --> 00:28:58.910
Rain got really into the sound effects on that keyboard.
雷恩当时特别沉迷于那个键盘上的音效。

733
00:28:59.130 --> 00:28:59.610
He did.
确实。

734
00:28:59.830 --> 00:29:00.410
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

735
00:29:00.450 --> 00:29:00.810
I do.
记得。

736
00:29:00.950 --> 00:29:04.490
So they had a keyboard for him, and they told him the different sounds the keyboard made.
他们给他准备了一个键盘，还告诉了他键盘能发出的各种声音。

737
00:29:04.650 --> 00:29:07.770
This is like handing a child, like, a keyboard.
这就像是给小孩子递了一个键盘一样。

738
00:29:08.050 --> 00:29:13.490
Or it's like, even when you give Rain a microphone, get ready, because he's going to have a lot of bits.
或者说，就算你给雷恩一个麦克风，也要做好准备，因为他会玩出很多花样。

739
00:29:13.490 --> 00:29:17.870
And they told him he could play it whenever he wanted during Michael's speeches.
他们告诉他，在迈克尔演讲的时候，他随时都可以弹。

740
00:29:17.990 --> 00:29:19.210
And did he ever?
他弹了吗？

741
00:29:19.410 --> 00:29:25.070
I mean, right out of the gate when Michael's like, well, Stanley, I can't wait to meet
我的意思是，刚一开始，当迈克尔说，好吧，斯坦利，我迫不及待想见见

742
00:29:25.070 --> 00:29:25.450
your wife.
你的妻子了。

743
00:29:25.530 --> 00:29:27.950
And he's like, I'm holding her hand right now.
然后他说，我现在正牵着她的手呢。

744
00:29:27.950 --> 00:29:31.770
So, like, that was Rain improviser, like, brr, brr.
所以，那是雷恩即兴发挥的，比如，嘟嘟，嘟嘟。

745
00:29:31.930 --> 00:29:32.170
Yeah.
没错。

746
00:29:32.370 --> 00:29:34.190
That was just Rain having fun on the keyboard.
那纯粹是雷恩在键盘上玩得开心。

747
00:29:34.430 --> 00:29:38.430
There was also an, oh, yeah, that he used to play.
还有一个他经常用的“哦，耶”的音效。

748
00:29:38.590 --> 00:29:39.330
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

749
00:29:39.430 --> 00:29:42.650
And Rain kept doing it at the most inappropriate moments.
雷恩总是在最不合时宜的时候用那个音效。

750
00:29:42.690 --> 00:29:46.010
And that was the thing that would make Steve break more than anything else.
那也是最容易让史蒂夫笑场的东西。

751
00:29:46.110 --> 00:29:48.870
It wasn't the fart noise or the trumpet sounds.
那不是放屁声或小号声。

752
00:29:49.050 --> 00:29:51.010
It was that, oh, yeah, button.
是那个“哦，耶”的按钮。

753
00:29:51.010 --> 00:29:54.930
And there was one time where Steve broke down laughing.
有一次史蒂夫笑得停不下来。

754
00:29:54.930 --> 00:29:56.410
It felt like 10 minutes.
感觉像过了10分钟一样。

755
00:29:56.490 --> 00:29:57.710
He could not get it back.
他怎么也停不下来。

756
00:29:57.790 --> 00:29:58.890
He doubled over.
他笑得腰都直不起来了。

757
00:29:59.070 --> 00:30:03.270
We had to stop filming because he got so tickled because Rain kept hitting that, oh, yeah, button.
我们不得不停止拍摄，因为他被雷恩一直按那个“哦，耶”按钮给逗乐了。

758
00:30:03.510 --> 00:30:04.890
And Steve never breaks.
史蒂夫从不笑场。

759
00:30:05.150 --> 00:30:06.550
He is a rock.
他就像块磐石。

760
00:30:06.650 --> 00:30:08.290
He and Oscar are the two.
他和奥斯卡是唯二的两个。

761
00:30:08.490 --> 00:30:08.750
Oh.
哦。

762
00:30:08.850 --> 00:30:10.590
It is very hard to make either of them break.
要让他们俩笑场真的很难。

763
00:30:10.710 --> 00:30:12.990
Oh, I would say they were statues for a long time.
哦，我会说他们俩很长一段时间里就像雕像一样。

764
00:30:13.070 --> 00:30:14.350
I was like, Oscar, are you a robot?
我当时心想，奥斯卡，你是机器人吗？

765
00:30:14.590 --> 00:30:15.890
Let's get into the awards.
我们来聊聊颁奖环节吧。

766
00:30:16.230 --> 00:30:19.150
There were seven Dundies given out at this awards.
这次颁奖典礼一共颁发了七个邓迪奖。

767
00:30:19.150 --> 00:30:22.290
I'm sure there were more given out, but what we witnessed were seven.
我肯定还有更多奖项，但我们看到的只有七个。

768
00:30:22.570 --> 00:30:27.090
There was the busiest beaver, which was the bushiest beaver to Phyllis.
有一个“最忙碌海狸奖”，其实是颁给菲利斯的“最毛茸茸海狸奖”。

769
00:30:27.470 --> 00:30:30.970
There was hottest in the office to Ryan the Temp, awkward.
还有一个颁给临时工瑞安的“办公室最火辣奖”，真尴尬。

770
00:30:31.370 --> 00:30:39.430
There was the tight ass award given to my character because not only is she's everybody's favorite stickler, she also has a great caboose.
还有一个“死板奖”颁给了我的角色，因为她不仅是大家最讨厌的死板鬼，而且她还有个很棒的屁股。

771
00:30:39.610 --> 00:30:46.970
The spicy curry award given to Kelly, and it was actually a bowling award because they had run out of the little men holding briefcases.
颁给凯莉的“辛辣咖喱奖”，其实那是个保龄球奖杯，因为他们用完了那种拿着公文包的小人奖杯。

772
