So David and I improvised a fight that we were having, and then they used it.
所以大卫和我即兴发挥了一段我们吵架的内容，然后他们就用了。

931
00:36:39.600 --> 00:36:39.900
Yeah.
是啊。

932
00:36:40.100 --> 00:36:41.200
So that was so crazy.
那真是太疯狂了。

933
00:36:41.440 --> 00:36:42.060
That is crazy.
确实很疯狂。

934
00:36:42.060 --> 00:36:44.980
And I love what Pam said when she was like, you know, if you had listened, you would have
我喜欢帕姆说的那句，你知道，如果你当时有在听，你就

935
00:36:44.980 --> 00:36:45.500
known that.
会知道了。

936
00:36:47.720 --> 00:36:51.480
But I was like, when Roy grabbed your arm, I was like, hey, hey now.
但我当时心想，当罗伊抓住你胳膊的时候，我心想，嘿，嘿，住手。

937
00:36:51.900 --> 00:36:52.420
I know.
我知道。

938
00:36:52.720 --> 00:36:56.380
He gets a little physical with her sometimes with the grabbing of the arm.
他有时候确实会动手动脚，比如抓胳膊之类的。

939
00:36:56.500 --> 00:36:57.480
Someone mentioned that.
有人提过这一点。

940
00:36:57.760 --> 00:36:59.080
And he's a big guy.
而且他是个大块头。

941
00:36:59.200 --> 00:36:59.760
He is.
确实是。

942
00:36:59.980 --> 00:37:04.540
So you sort of really see in that moment that Pam is just fed up, and she wants to stay,
所以在那一刻你真的能看出帕姆已经受够了，她想留下来，

943
00:37:04.640 --> 00:37:06.000
and she wants to be with her friends.
她想和她的朋友们在一起。

944
00:37:06.480 --> 00:37:09.160
And I think she wants to be with another person.
而且我觉得她想和另一个人在一起。

945
00:37:09.300 --> 00:37:10.440
I don't know what you're talking about.
我不知道你在说什么。

946
00:37:10.520 --> 00:37:10.700
Yeah.
是啊。

947
00:37:10.800 --> 00:37:15.900
I think she wants to be with Jim, who she sits down at a table with.
我觉得她想和吉姆在一起，她坐到了他那桌。

948
00:37:15.900 --> 00:37:16.480
I know.
我知道。

949
00:37:16.540 --> 00:37:18.720
And the look on his face when you come back in.
当你走回来时，他脸上的表情。

950
00:37:18.920 --> 00:37:19.160
Oh.
噢。

951
00:37:19.320 --> 00:37:20.200
He is so delighted.
他非常高兴。

952
00:37:20.200 --> 00:37:22.020
She starts drinking his beer immediately.
她立刻开始喝他的啤酒。

953
00:37:22.200 --> 00:37:22.580
I know.
我知道。

954
00:37:22.860 --> 00:37:27.080
Then she orders her own drinks, and it leads us into a famous line.
然后她点了自己的酒，这引出了我们的一句名台词。

955
00:37:27.220 --> 00:37:28.680
Who knew it would be this famous?
谁能想到它会这么出名呢？

956
00:37:28.780 --> 00:37:28.940
What?
什么？

957
00:37:28.940 --> 00:37:30.200
Written by Mindy Kaling.
由敏迪·卡灵编写。

958
00:37:30.500 --> 00:37:32.080
Look what I have on my note card.
看看我的笔记卡上写了什么。

959
00:37:32.240 --> 00:37:33.600
It's like second drink.
就像是“第二杯酒”。

960
00:37:33.920 --> 00:37:34.860
Second drink.
第二杯酒。

961
00:37:35.300 --> 00:37:35.740
Yes.
是的。

962
00:37:35.740 --> 00:37:40.360
And Andrew Nelson asked, did you add LibSecond drink, or was it scripted?
安德鲁·尼尔森问，是你加了“第二杯酒”这句台词，还是剧本里写的？

963
00:37:40.480 --> 00:37:41.380
It was scripted.
是剧本里写的。

964
00:37:41.800 --> 00:37:44.240
And a lot of people asked about, what are we really drinking?
还有很多人问，我们到底在喝什么？

965
00:37:44.640 --> 00:37:45.980
Is it really alcohol?
真的是酒吗？

966
00:37:46.400 --> 00:37:46.840
No.
不是。

967
00:37:47.320 --> 00:37:47.520
No.
不是。

968
00:37:47.520 --> 00:37:48.880
It would be so wasted.
那样的话早就醉得不行了。

969
00:37:48.880 --> 00:37:55.180
Also, it looks like something from, like, a Nickelodeon slime, like, award show.
而且，它看起来就像尼克儿童频道颁奖礼上的那种史莱姆粘液。

970
00:37:55.380 --> 00:37:58.820
Because, like, have you—do you see, like, if you look at Meredith's drink, it's like
因为，你看，如果你仔细看梅雷迪思的酒，它是那种

971
00:37:58.820 --> 00:38:00.060
a neon green.
霓虹绿色的。

972
00:38:00.360 --> 00:38:00.620
Yeah.
是啊。

973
00:38:00.720 --> 00:38:01.520
What was she drinking?
她当时喝的是什么？

974
00:38:01.780 --> 00:38:02.300
I don't know.
我不知道。

975
00:38:02.340 --> 00:38:05.520
But I think they really wanted the drinks to pop so you could see them.
但我认为他们确实希望酒的颜色鲜艳点，这样你们才能看清楚。

976
00:38:05.560 --> 00:38:07.820
And so they added a lot of, like, food dye and things.
所以他们加了很多食用色素之类的东西。

977
00:38:07.980 --> 00:38:10.780
Well, the beer is usually just non-alcoholic beer.
嗯，啤酒通常只是无酒精啤酒。

978
00:38:10.880 --> 00:38:12.560
So the beer actually tastes like beer.
所以啤酒喝起来确实像啤酒。

979
00:38:12.700 --> 00:38:13.600
And you feel bloaty.
而且你会觉得肚子胀。

980
00:38:13.600 --> 00:38:14.260
Yeah.
是啊。

981
00:38:14.460 --> 00:38:16.740
And I don't like beer, and I don't like the taste of beer.
我不喜欢啤酒，也不喜欢啤酒的味道。

982
00:38:16.780 --> 00:38:19.500
So I hate it whenever I have to drink it on camera, because bleh.
所以我很讨厌在镜头前喝它，因为太难喝了。

983
00:38:19.940 --> 00:38:24.460
And then other drinks, like wine, it's usually watered-down juice.
至于其他饮料，比如红酒，通常是兑了水的果汁。

984
00:38:24.700 --> 00:38:25.580
Cranberry juice.
蔓越莓汁。

985
00:38:26.320 --> 00:38:27.040
Apple juice.
苹果汁。

986
00:38:27.120 --> 00:38:27.300
Yeah.
是啊。

987
00:38:27.860 --> 00:38:30.020
And then the other drinks are anything.
至于其他的饮料，什么都有可能。

988
00:38:30.420 --> 00:38:33.640
Sometimes it's just water with a little food coloring in it.
有时候就只是加了点食用色素的水。

989
00:38:33.680 --> 00:38:37.000
Or, like, if it is supposed to look like a bourbon or something, it could just be tea.
或者，如果需要看起来像波本威士忌之类的，可能就是茶。

990
00:38:37.480 --> 00:38:38.120
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

991
00:38:38.420 --> 00:38:38.780
Yeah.
是啊。

992
00:38:38.880 --> 00:38:41.260
Sometimes they'll brew you some tea and pour it over ice.
有时候他们会为你泡点茶，然后倒在冰块上。

993
00:38:41.460 --> 00:38:43.120
I'm actually happy when you have that.
有这种饮料的时候我其实挺开心的。

994
00:38:43.120 --> 00:38:45.720
Like, if you have a Long Island iced tea in it, you're just drinking an iced tea.
比如，如果杯子里装的是长岛冰茶，你其实就是在喝冰茶。

995
00:38:45.900 --> 00:38:46.040
Yeah.
是啊。

996
00:38:46.320 --> 00:38:51.240
Sam just pulled up, for you guys listening, a whole page on the internet of just me rolling
山姆刚才调出了一整页互联网上的图片，对于正在收听的各位，那上面全是我翻白眼

997
00:38:51.240 --> 00:38:52.960
my eyes and looking snarky.
和一脸刻薄的样子。

998
00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:57.720
So as Angela Martin, I guess there's a lot of snarky eye roll options out there.
所以作为安吉拉·马丁，我想网上有很多我翻白眼的刻薄表情包。

999
00:38:57.840 --> 00:38:58.960
Or just snarky looks.
或者仅仅是刻薄的表情。

1000
00:38:59.220 --> 00:39:00.840
They're not limited to the Dundies.
它们可不局限于邓迪奖颁奖礼。

1001
00:39:01.020 --> 00:39:02.220
Okay, Sam, take it down.
好了，萨姆，停一下。

1002
00:39:02.420 --> 00:39:05.180
I can't look at myself rolling my eyes at myself.
我没法看自己在那儿翻白眼的样子。

1003
00:39:05.340 --> 00:39:11.160
So now we get into the tender moment, where Michael is desperately trying to keep the Dundies
现在到了那个温情的时刻，迈克尔拼命想让邓迪奖颁奖礼继续下去，

1004
00:39:11.160 --> 00:39:14.280
going, and the guys at the bar start to heckle him.
而吧台那边的人开始起哄嘲讽他。

1005
00:39:14.420 --> 00:39:14.680
Yeah.
没错。

1006
00:39:14.940 --> 00:39:17.000
And he's so wounded.
他当时真的很受伤。

1007
00:39:17.860 --> 00:39:19.840
And Pam won't have it.
而帕姆看不下去了。

1008
00:39:20.180 --> 00:39:21.660
Well, I think it's that moment.
嗯，我觉得就是那一刻。

1009
00:39:21.840 --> 00:39:28.220
Even there's a look that comes across Jim's face of like, ooh, like, that's mean, you know?
吉姆脸上甚至闪过一种表情，好像在说，噢，这也太刻薄了，你知道吗？

1010
00:39:28.380 --> 00:39:28.540
Yeah.
没错。

1011
00:39:28.580 --> 00:39:33.320
And it's sort of that thing of like, you know, your creepy cousin that creeps everyone out,
那种感觉就像，你知道，你有个让所有人都觉得毛骨悚然的怪表亲，

1012
00:39:33.460 --> 00:39:35.460
but you have to take up for them because they're your cousin.
但你又不得不护着他，因为他是你的表亲。

1013
00:39:35.460 --> 00:39:40.380
It's like that moment of like, okay, he's like family, and we get to like make fun of
就像那一刻，好吧，他就像家人一样，我们可以取笑他，

1014
00:39:40.380 --> 00:39:41.340
him, but no one else can.
但别人不行。

1015
00:39:41.520 --> 00:39:42.100
That's right.
说得对。

1016
00:39:42.420 --> 00:39:47.780
And Pam starts chanting Dundies and getting people to rally around him.
然后帕姆开始带头高喊“邓迪奖”，号召大家支持他。

1017
00:39:48.000 --> 00:39:49.320
And I love that.
我太喜欢这一幕了。

1018
00:39:49.460 --> 00:39:52.460
And this is a little bit the relationship between Pam and Michael.
这多少体现了帕姆和迈克尔之间的关系。

1019
00:39:52.720 --> 00:39:57.560
This is the way that she shows up for him, the way he shows up for her at her art show
这就是她支持他的方式，就像后来在她的画展上，他支持她一样。

1020
00:39:57.560 --> 00:39:57.920
later.
后来。

1021
00:39:58.100 --> 00:39:58.300
Yeah.
没错。

1022
00:39:58.940 --> 00:40:01.780
Like in their lowest moments, they are there for one another.
就像在他们最失落的时候，他们都会陪伴在彼此身边。

1023
00:40:01.780 --> 00:40:06.280
When Pam gives him a hug when she gets her Dundie, his face is so precious.
当帕姆领奖时拥抱他，他那表情真是太珍贵了。

1024
00:40:06.600 --> 00:40:09.580
He's just like, it's like the whole night was made in that moment.
他看起来就像是，那一刻让他觉得整晚的努力都值了。

1025
00:40:09.780 --> 00:40:13.200
Well, Pam accepting her Dundie is another famous line.
嗯，帕姆领奖时说的那句台词也很经典。

1026
00:40:13.280 --> 00:40:13.620
Yes.
是的。

1027
00:40:14.020 --> 00:40:16.360
I feel God in this Chili's tonight.
今晚我在这家辣椒餐厅感受到了上帝的存在。

1028
00:40:16.840 --> 00:40:17.240
Aw.
噢。

1029
00:40:17.280 --> 00:40:18.240
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1030
00:40:18.820 --> 00:40:24.060
So when I rewatched this, there was this moment I wrote on my note card because when you say
所以当我重温这一集时，我特意在笔记里记下了一个瞬间，因为当你提到

1031
00:40:24.060 --> 00:40:27.860
I'd like to thank God for this Dundie, it cuts to Jim.
“我要感谢上帝让我获得这个邓迪奖”时，镜头切到了吉姆。

1032
00:40:27.860 --> 00:40:32.960
And Jim's reaction to you thanking God for your Dundie is one of the best moments for
吉姆对你感谢上帝获得邓迪奖的反应，是我认为整集中

1033
00:40:32.960 --> 00:40:34.000
me of the whole episode.
最棒的时刻之一。

1034
00:40:34.200 --> 00:40:35.700
It is just so sweet.
真的太甜了。

1035
00:40:35.800 --> 00:40:40.040
He's just looking at you like, oh, my sweet little drunk friend.
他看着你的眼神就像在说，噢，我那可爱又喝醉的小朋友。

1036
00:40:40.080 --> 00:40:40.940
I love you.
我爱你。

1037
00:40:41.100 --> 00:40:46.580
Well, I talked to Mindy about this on the day, and she had told me that Greg did not have
嗯，当时我和敏迪聊过这件事，她告诉我，格雷格对帕姆感谢上帝领奖这个桥段

1038
00:40:46.580 --> 00:40:50.620
total confidence in Pam thanking God for her Dundie, but we were going to do it anyway.
并不是完全有信心，但我们还是决定要这么演。

1039
00:40:50.820 --> 00:40:52.800
He was a little bit like, I don't totally get it.
他当时有点觉得，我不太明白为什么要这么做。

1040
00:40:52.800 --> 00:40:58.560
And she's like, no, you know, like whenever people win awards or they have like big sports
然后她说，不，你知道，就像人们获奖或者在体育比赛中

1041
00:40:58.560 --> 00:41:00.800
moments, a lot of times they thank God.
取得重大时刻时，很多时候他们都会感谢上帝。

1042
00:41:00.960 --> 00:41:02.640
And I asked her, I said, but how do I do it?
我问她，我说，那我该怎么演呢？

1043
00:41:02.700 --> 00:41:05.060
Because, and she said, you do it totally sincerely.
因为，她说，你要表现得非常真诚。

1044
00:41:05.400 --> 00:41:05.620
Yeah.
没错。

1045
00:41:05.740 --> 00:41:10.660
She's like, you really are like sincerely thankful and grateful for your Dundie tonight.
她说，你要表现得真的非常感谢，非常感激今晚获得的这个邓迪奖。

1046
00:41:10.660 --> 00:41:14.780
It totally made sense to me because I felt like drunk Pam thinks this is what you do
这对我来说完全说得通，因为我觉得喝醉后的帕姆认为这就是领奖时

1047
00:41:14.780 --> 00:41:15.520
when you win an award.
该做的事。

1048
00:41:15.720 --> 00:41:15.880
That's right.
没错。

1049
00:41:15.980 --> 00:41:19.100
You take a moment, you thank God, then you scream.
你要停顿一下，感谢上帝，然后尖叫。

1050
00:41:19.220 --> 00:41:19.520
Woohoo!
呜呼！

1051
00:41:19.520 --> 00:41:21.860
Yeah, and I loved it so much.
没错，我太喜欢那一幕了。

1052
00:41:22.020 --> 00:41:29.020
And then after this, after she gets her Dundie, Pam kisses Jim on the lips.
在那之后，帕姆领完邓迪奖，就亲了吉姆的嘴唇。

1053
00:41:29.200 --> 00:41:29.800
I know.
我知道。

1054
00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:30.520
I know.
我知道。

1055
00:41:30.600 --> 00:41:31.320
Was that weird?
那很奇怪吗？

1056
00:41:31.620 --> 00:41:33.500
Well, this was a big fan question.
嗯，这是粉丝们问得最多的一个问题。

1057
00:41:33.700 --> 00:41:39.600
Caitlin asked, do you consider this episode as Pam and Jim's first kiss, or do you think
凯特琳问，你们认为这一集是帕姆和吉姆的初吻吗，还是你们觉得

1058
00:41:39.600 --> 00:41:40.680
it's casino night?
是在赌场之夜那集？

1059
00:41:41.360 --> 00:41:44.020
I did not consider this their first kiss.
我没觉得那是他们的初吻。

1060
00:41:44.180 --> 00:41:44.720
I did.
我倒是觉得是。

1061
00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:45.640
John did.
约翰也觉得是。

1062
00:41:45.860 --> 00:41:46.580
I disagree.
我不同意。

1063
00:41:46.580 --> 00:41:49.860
I consider it, you planted one on him.
我觉得那是你主动凑上去亲他的。

1064
00:41:50.680 --> 00:41:53.800
The intention there was that it was accidental.
当时的设计是那纯属意外。

1065
00:41:54.380 --> 00:41:57.660
The intention was that Pam was going for his cheek.
帕姆本意是想亲他的脸颊。

1066
00:41:57.820 --> 00:41:58.160
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1067
00:41:58.300 --> 00:42:04.720
And it was one of those moments where you, he moved his head in a way that I wasn't expecting,
当时的情况是，他移动头部的方向我没预料到，

1068
00:42:04.720 --> 00:42:07.360
and I'm drunk, and I just followed through.
而且我喝醉了，就顺势亲下去了。

1069
00:42:07.640 --> 00:42:10.160
That was what was in my head as Pam.
作为帕姆，我当时心里是这么想的。

1070
00:42:10.420 --> 00:42:13.520
So I wasn't thinking that I was intending to kiss his lips.
所以我并没有打算要亲他的嘴唇。

1071
00:42:13.520 --> 00:42:16.460
And so Pam kind of doesn't register it.
所以帕姆当时其实没反应过来。

1072
00:42:16.740 --> 00:42:17.460
That was me.
那是我的想法。

1073
00:42:18.020 --> 00:42:23.280
John said that Jim, who is not drunk, was very aware that they just kissed on the lips.
约翰说吉姆当时没喝醉，他非常清楚他们刚刚亲了嘴。

1074
00:42:23.360 --> 00:42:25.820
And this was a whole conversation that we had off camera.
我们私下里还专门讨论过这件事。

1075
00:42:26.040 --> 00:42:27.120
I agree with him, though.
不过我同意他的看法。

1076
00:42:27.220 --> 00:42:28.160
And I see both sides.
两边的观点我都能理解。

1077
00:42:28.280 --> 00:42:31.680
I see as a drunk person, you just kind of hug and you're a little sloppy.
我理解作为一个醉酒的人，你可能只是想拥抱一下，动作有点笨拙。

1078
00:42:31.980 --> 00:42:32.320
Yeah.
没错。

1079
00:42:32.520 --> 00:42:36.780
But I see for him as a sober person, this person he's in love with just kissed him.
但我也理解对他而言，作为一个清醒的人，他深爱的人刚刚亲了他。

1080
00:42:37.600 --> 00:42:38.040
Yeah.
没错。

1081
00:42:38.040 --> 00:42:40.560
But it was unintentional on Pam's part.
但对帕姆来说，那确实不是故意的。

1082
00:42:40.660 --> 00:42:41.020
I know.
我知道。

1083
00:42:41.060 --> 00:42:41.980
In her mind.
在她心里是这样。

1084
00:42:42.120 --> 00:42:42.540
I know.
我知道。

1085
00:42:42.700 --> 00:42:47.620
But a lot of people wrote in and said, oh, my gosh, why didn't everyone in the office,
但很多人写信问，天哪，为什么办公室里的其他人，

1086
00:42:47.760 --> 00:42:50.660
why wasn't this a big gossipy moment?
为什么这没成为一个八卦焦点？

1087
00:42:50.940 --> 00:42:54.020
They know Pam's engaged, and they all witnessed her kiss Jim.
他们都知道帕姆订婚了，而且都亲眼目睹她亲了吉姆。

1088
00:42:54.460 --> 00:42:59.280
And in my mind, it was because it wasn't really a kiss.
在我看来，那是因为那根本算不上一个吻。

1089
00:42:59.400 --> 00:43:00.160
It wasn't a...
那不是……

1090
00:43:00.700 --> 00:43:04.020
Oh, well, in my mind, everyone was talking about it at work.
噢，好吧，在我看来，大家在公司里肯定都在议论这件事。

1091
00:43:04.020 --> 00:43:04.920
Trust me.
相信我。

1092
00:43:05.720 --> 00:43:10.940
Because I tell you what, Angela Martin was sitting with Phyllis in a booth when that happened.
因为我告诉你，安吉拉·马丁当时就和菲利斯坐在隔间里，目睹了那一幕。

1093
00:43:11.180 --> 00:43:13.140
And I'm pretty sure she was like, mm-hmm.
我敢肯定她当时肯定在想，嗯哼。

1094
00:43:13.380 --> 00:43:18.100
Did you see the office mattress just to smooch someone else?
你看到那个办公室荡妇又去亲别人了吗？

1095
00:43:18.260 --> 00:43:20.400
Well, I have another fan question for you then.
好吧，那我这儿还有一个粉丝提问。

1096
00:43:20.600 --> 00:43:21.620
This one is from Amy.
这个问题来自艾米。

1097
00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:29.080
She said, at the end, when you drive Pam home, in my mind, Angela would be so disgusted by Pam's
她说，最后你开车送帕姆回家时，我觉得安吉拉应该会对帕姆的行为感到非常恶心，

1098
00:43:29.080 --> 00:43:31.400
behavior, it seems odd that she would give her a ride.
她还会送她回家，这看起来很奇怪。

1099
00:43:31.400 --> 00:43:36.640
Well, let me tell you, Amy, if you watch the deleted scenes, because I did, you will see
好吧，艾米，让我告诉你，如果你看了删减片段——因为我看了——你就会发现

1100
00:43:36.640 --> 00:43:41.600
that Angela Martin has a talking head where she is the company's designated driver.
安吉拉·马丁有一个采访镜头，提到她是公司的指定代驾。

1101
00:43:42.100 --> 00:43:46.740
And you would know that Angela Martin would take this very serious as the safety officer
而且你知道安吉拉·马丁作为邓德·米夫林的安保官，会非常认真地对待这件事。

1102
00:43:46.740 --> 00:43:48.120
for Dunder Mifflin.
对于邓德·米夫林来说。

1103
00:43:48.240 --> 00:43:52.020
And I have this talking head where Angela goes on to say, and you know what?
我还有一段采访片段，安吉拉在里面接着说，你知道吗？

1104
00:43:52.160 --> 00:43:53.840
No one gives me any gas money.
没人给我油钱。

1105
00:43:53.960 --> 00:43:55.760
And everyone lives all over.
大家住得又到处都是。

1106
00:43:56.020 --> 00:43:57.100
It's very expensive.
这太贵了。

1107
00:43:58.220 --> 00:43:58.780
Wow.
哇。

1108
00:43:59.040 --> 00:44:00.320
That is gold.
那真是太经典了。

1109
00:44:00.320 --> 00:44:02.220
So she's always the martyr.
所以她总是扮演那个受难者的角色。

1110
00:44:02.420 --> 00:44:04.880
She's doing her job, but no one gives her gas money.
她在做自己的工作，但没人给她油钱。

1111
00:44:04.980 --> 00:44:07.980
And she has to drive these drunks around, but she's the designated driver.
她还得载着这些醉鬼，但她是指定驾驶员。

1112
00:44:07.980 --> 00:44:09.480
And so she has to do it.
所以她不得不这么做。

1113
00:44:09.560 --> 00:44:12.740
So not only did Pam probably not give her any gas money.
所以帕姆不仅可能没给她油钱。

1114
00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:13.260
Yeah.
没错。

1115
00:44:13.660 --> 00:44:17.520
She was very disappointed in her behavior.
她对帕姆的行为感到非常失望。

1116
00:44:17.800 --> 00:44:21.840
Angela quietly judged her the whole drive and probably told her, you need to make some
安吉拉在整个车程中都在默默地评判她，可能还对她说，你需要做出一些

1117
00:44:21.840 --> 00:44:23.040
new life choices.
新的人生选择。

1118
00:44:23.360 --> 00:44:25.760
Amy also wanted to know, was that really you driving?
艾米还想知道，开车的人真的是你吗？

1119
00:44:25.760 --> 00:44:27.040
Yes, it was.
是的，是我。

1120
00:44:27.040 --> 00:44:30.580
At 20 minutes, two seconds in the car, you see my shoulder.
在车里20分02秒的时候，你能看到我的肩膀。

1121
00:44:30.960 --> 00:44:32.220
Now, here's the thing.
现在，问题是这样的。

1122
00:44:32.340 --> 00:44:33.840
They wanted me every time in the car.
他们每次都想让我待在车里。

1123
00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:35.060
You got in with me every time.
你每次都跟我一起上车。

1124
00:44:35.180 --> 00:44:35.720
I pulled away.
我开车离开。

1125
00:44:35.880 --> 00:44:38.740
And then I would back up and we'd do the scene over a few times.
然后我会倒车，我们把那个场景重拍了几次。

1126
00:44:39.020 --> 00:44:44.540
And I had a front row seat watching Pam and Jim have that sort of very tender but awkward
我有幸坐在前排，看着帕姆和吉姆经历那种非常温柔但又尴尬的

1127
00:44:44.540 --> 00:44:48.520
moment where Pam has a question for him, but then notices the camera.
时刻，帕姆本来有个问题想问他，但随后注意到了摄像机。

1128
00:44:48.520 --> 00:44:51.600
I watched that whole thing over and over as you guys did it.
你们拍的时候，我把整个过程看了又看。

1129
00:44:51.680 --> 00:44:52.480
And it was so great.
那真是太棒了。

1130
00:44:52.620 --> 00:44:54.120
You guys did such a fantastic job.
你们表现得太出色了。

1131
00:44:54.460 --> 00:44:58.780
And when I re-watched it, part of me was like, well, why'd they have me in the car?
当我重看的时候，我心里想，好吧，他们为什么非要我待在车里？

1132
00:44:58.880 --> 00:45:00.300
You don't see me anyway.
反正你也看不见我。

1133
00:45:00.700 --> 00:45:01.700
But they didn't know.
但他们当时不知道。

1134
00:45:01.800 --> 00:45:04.820
As you know, with our show, we always had an A camera and a B camera.
如你所知，在我们的剧中，我们总是有A机位和B机位。

1135
00:45:04.940 --> 00:45:07.100
And they would be sort of carving up the scene.
他们会把场景拆解开来拍摄。

1136
00:45:07.200 --> 00:45:10.160
And there might be this moment where they whipped around and could have seen me.
可能会有那么一瞬间，他们镜头一转，就有可能拍到我。

1137
00:45:10.280 --> 00:45:13.120
So they wanted to make sure I was there just in case.
所以他们想确保我在场，以防万一。

1138
00:45:13.240 --> 00:45:14.700
And I was happy to be there.
我很乐意待在那里。

1139
00:45:15.780 --> 00:45:19.820
Yeah, a lot of times they would use a double for that in other shows.
是啊，很多其他剧组在这种情况下会用替身。

1140
00:45:19.820 --> 00:45:22.200
But in our show, we were our own doubles.
但在我们的剧里，我们就是自己的替身。

1141
00:45:22.460 --> 00:45:22.800
That's right.
没错。

1142
00:45:22.800 --> 00:45:27.020
Because as a documentary, you really never knew where that second camera would end up landing.
因为作为一部纪录片，你真的永远不知道第二个机位会落在哪里。

1143
00:45:27.060 --> 00:45:28.440
And you could end up on camera.
你随时可能入镜。

1144
00:45:28.580 --> 00:45:34.620
I was asked, is that a cat air freshener hanging from your rear view mirror in your car?
有人问我，你车里后视镜上挂的是猫咪形状的空气清新剂吗？

1145
00:45:35.000 --> 00:45:35.600
Is it?
是吗？

1146
00:45:35.800 --> 00:45:38.260
It looks like it could be a cat or a tree.
看起来既像猫又像棵树。

1147
00:45:38.440 --> 00:45:39.280
Guys, I don't know.
伙计们，我不知道。

1148
00:45:39.420 --> 00:45:40.520
I tried to zoom in on it.
我试着放大看了看。

1149
00:45:40.660 --> 00:45:41.700
Oh, I hope it's a cat.
哦，我希望那是只猫。

1150
00:45:41.780 --> 00:45:42.460
I hope it's a green.
我希望那是绿色的。

1151
00:45:42.460 --> 00:45:43.420
Let's call it a cat.
我们就叫它猫吧。

1152
00:45:43.420 --> 00:45:44.340
I hope it's a green cat.
我希望它是只绿色的猫。

1153
00:45:44.340 --> 00:45:47.000
Green cat doesn't sound right now, Angela.
绿色的猫现在听起来不太对劲，安吉拉。

1154
00:45:47.220 --> 00:45:50.800
I know, but maybe it was a Christmas cat that I held on to.
我知道，但也许那是我留着的一只圣诞猫。

1155
00:45:51.140 --> 00:45:51.700
Not sure.
不太确定。

1156
00:45:52.100 --> 00:45:57.160
Something we haven't talked about is the scene where Pam falls off the stool because she is so drunk.
我们还没聊到帕姆因为喝得太醉从凳子上摔下来的那一幕。

1157
00:45:57.600 --> 00:46:00.380
And this leads me into a fan question.
这让我想到了一个粉丝提问。

1158
00:46:00.740 --> 00:46:00.920
Okay.
好的。

1159
00:46:01.100 --> 00:46:04.800
Matt Sheldon asked, how did you get Chili's to cooperate with this idea?
马特·谢尔顿问，你们是怎么让Chili's餐厅配合这个想法的？

1160
00:46:05.660 --> 00:46:10.100
Well, they were on the fence and we almost weren't allowed to film there, remember?
嗯，他们当时很犹豫，我们差点就没被允许在那里拍摄，还记得吗？

1161
00:46:10.380 --> 00:46:11.740
Well, here's what happened.
嗯，事情是这样的。

1162
00:46:12.560 --> 00:46:16.600
Originally, in the script, Pam vomits all over the bar.
最初的剧本里，帕姆在吧台上吐了一地。

1163
00:46:16.760 --> 00:46:18.180
She does not fall off the stool.
她并没有从凳子上摔下来。

1164
00:46:18.360 --> 00:46:19.220
She is listening to Jim.
她在听吉姆说话。

1165
00:46:19.340 --> 00:46:20.060
She is nodding.
她在点头。

1166
00:46:20.180 --> 00:46:21.140
And then she vomits.
然后她就吐了。

1167
00:46:21.560 --> 00:46:23.700
And we had been filming for two days.
我们当时已经拍了两天了。

1168
00:46:23.900 --> 00:46:24.280
Right.
没错。

1169
00:46:24.280 --> 00:46:28.620
And I guess suddenly they had had Chili's permission.
我想他们突然就得到了Chili's的许可。

1170
00:46:28.860 --> 00:46:30.360
Chili's helped build the Chili's.
Chili's帮忙搭建了那个Chili's餐厅场景。

1171
00:46:30.480 --> 00:46:34.120
And someone at Chili's read the script, finally.
然后Chili's那边终于有人读了剧本。

1172
00:46:34.360 --> 00:46:35.060
Well, I guess—
嗯，我想——

1173
00:46:35.060 --> 00:46:36.120
And freaked out.
然后就吓坏了。

1174
00:46:36.300 --> 00:46:38.300
I read the script wasn't fully complete.
我读到过剧本当时还没完全写完。

1175
00:46:38.500 --> 00:46:40.100
You know, they hadn't done their second pass.
你知道，他们还没进行第二轮修改。

1176
00:46:40.240 --> 00:46:42.820
And so Chili's had not gotten all of the scenes.
所以Chili's那边还没拿到所有的场景剧本。

1177
00:46:42.920 --> 00:46:47.440
And so they didn't have the scene where Pam vomited and all of this happened.
所以他们没看到帕姆呕吐以及后面发生的一切那一幕。

1178
00:46:47.600 --> 00:46:50.340
Well, once they read that, they shut down the production.
好吧，他们一读到那段，就叫停了拍摄。

1179
00:46:50.340 --> 00:46:50.980
Yes.
是的。

1180
00:46:51.100 --> 00:46:51.980
And we thought, what?
我们当时想，什么？

1181
00:46:52.080 --> 00:46:53.520
They said, no way.
他们说，没门。

1182
00:46:53.780 --> 00:46:54.120
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1183
00:46:54.640 --> 00:47:00.800
We—they were very nervous about the drinking and the drunkenness and the sort of way that
我们——他们对饮酒和醉酒的状态非常紧张，觉得那种方式

1184
00:47:00.800 --> 00:47:02.200
that might reflect on Chili's.
可能会对Chili's的形象产生负面影响。

1185
00:47:02.200 --> 00:47:05.360
So Greg and Mindy started scrambling.
所以格雷格和敏迪开始紧急补救。

1186
00:47:05.680 --> 00:47:11.300
And they came up with this idea that instead of vomiting, that Pam would fall off a stool.
他们想出了一个主意，把呕吐改成帕姆从凳子上摔下来。

1187
00:47:11.620 --> 00:47:12.000
Right.
没错。

1188
00:47:12.100 --> 00:47:15.160
And then also, I think it was Rain's idea to say, well, maybe Dwight could say, oh,
而且我还记得，是雷恩提议说，嗯，也许德怀特可以说，哦，

1189
00:47:15.220 --> 00:47:17.660
she's had a seizure and not the vomiting.
她是癫痫发作了，而不是呕吐。

1190
00:47:17.980 --> 00:47:24.060
And then the other part of it was that we had to write in a new element, which is that
然后另一部分就是我们必须加入一个新的情节，那就是

1191
00:47:24.060 --> 00:47:26.180
Pam was going to get banned from Chili's.
帕姆要被Chili's列入黑名单。

1192
00:47:26.180 --> 00:47:33.200
And the person who gives the speech in the episode was an actual Chili's manager franchise
剧集中发表讲话的那个人是真正的Chili's经理兼加盟商

1193
00:47:33.200 --> 00:47:34.900
owner named John Bossert.
名叫约翰·博塞特。

1194
00:47:35.120 --> 00:47:35.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1195
00:47:35.380 --> 00:47:36.680
He was not an actor.
他不是演员。

1196
00:47:37.200 --> 00:47:37.320
Right.
没错。

1197
00:47:37.320 --> 00:47:43.460
And they felt like by having an actual Chili's representative state very clearly the Chili's
他们觉得通过让真正的Chili's代表非常明确地陈述Chili's

1198
00:47:43.460 --> 00:47:45.220
policy against over-serving.
反对过度供酒的政策，

1199
00:47:45.360 --> 00:47:45.640
Right.
没错。

1200
00:47:45.820 --> 00:47:50.440
And banning Pam for life, then they allowed us to film the rest of the episode.
并终身禁止帕姆进入，他们才允许我们拍摄剩下的剧集。

1201
00:47:50.600 --> 00:47:50.880
Yes.
是的。

1202
00:47:50.980 --> 00:47:53.880
And also, they had Pam—they had you as Pam.
而且，他们让帕姆——他们让你演帕姆。

1203
00:47:54.300 --> 00:47:56.740
A waiter never brought you more drinks.
服务员再也没给你上过酒。

1204
00:47:56.740 --> 00:47:58.860
You were reaching on other people's tables.
你甚至去够别人桌上的酒。

1205
00:47:58.860 --> 00:48:01.120
So you were doing it, not Chili's.
所以是你自己干的，不是Chili's的问题。

1206
00:48:01.220 --> 00:48:02.060
And you know what?
你知道吗？

1207
00:48:02.060 --> 00:48:02.860
I think that's great.
我觉得这很棒。

1208
00:48:02.860 --> 00:48:08.240
I think that it was really important to Chili's that people know that they are responsible.
我觉得Chili's让人们知道他们会负责任，这一点非常重要。

1209
00:48:08.540 --> 00:48:09.860
And a family establishment.
而且是一家家庭式餐厅。

1210
00:48:10.000 --> 00:48:10.960
And a family establishment.
而且是一家家庭式餐厅。

1211
00:48:11.120 --> 00:48:11.220
Yeah.
没错。

1212
00:48:11.220 --> 00:48:17.320
And I love that John Bossert, an actual Chili's, like, owner, got to do that talking head.
我特别喜欢约翰·博塞特，一个真正的Chili's老板，能来做那个采访镜头。

1213
00:48:17.420 --> 00:48:19.140
I thought he did a fantastic job.
我觉得他表现得太棒了。

1214
00:48:19.140 --> 00:48:19.320
He did great.
他演得很好。

1215
00:48:19.500 --> 00:48:22.100
His look to camera when he's like, so she is banned.
他看向镜头时说“所以她被禁了”的那一下。

1216
00:48:22.280 --> 00:48:24.140
Like, his little look to camera was fantastic.
他看向镜头的那小眼神简直绝了。

1217
00:48:24.420 --> 00:48:30.160
And also, that aspect of Pam being banned for life was a wonderful thing that just grew into
而且，帕姆被终身禁入这一点也很棒，后来衍生出了

1218
00:48:30.160 --> 00:48:31.820
many more jokes and—
很多笑话，还有——

1219
00:48:31.820 --> 00:48:32.240
I know.
我知道。

1220
00:48:32.380 --> 00:48:32.900
I loved it.
我超喜欢。

1221
00:48:33.120 --> 00:48:36.420
I love that—Pam is, like, such, like, not a troublemaker.
我喜欢这一点——帕姆这种人，根本不是那种会惹麻烦的人。

1222
00:48:36.540 --> 00:48:39.740
And she's banned from, like, a nationwide chain.
结果她竟然被一家全国连锁店给禁了。

1223
00:48:39.980 --> 00:48:40.380
Yes.
没错。

1224
00:48:41.400 --> 00:48:45.100
As if there is such a system that could control that.
就好像真有那种能管得住这事的系统一样。

1225
00:48:45.240 --> 00:48:47.880
I have one card that's sort of around that area.
我这儿有一张卡片，内容差不多是关于这部分的。

1226
00:48:47.880 --> 00:48:49.340
So can I talk about it right now?
我现在能说吗？

1227
00:48:49.460 --> 00:48:49.820
Sure.
当然。

1228
00:48:49.980 --> 00:48:52.880
Once again, Rainn Wilson finds a way to take off his shirt.
雷恩·威尔森又一次找到了脱掉衬衫的机会。

1229
00:48:53.040 --> 00:48:54.960
Always taking off his shirt, Rainn Wilson.
雷恩·威尔森总是脱衬衫。

1230
00:48:54.980 --> 00:48:57.420
We get to see his beautiful, white, fleshy belly.
我们得以看到他那白皙、肉嘟嘟的美丽肚皮。

1231
00:48:57.640 --> 00:48:59.460
Because somehow, that's going to help save Pam.
因为不知怎么的，这就能帮到帕姆。

1232
00:48:59.620 --> 00:49:01.220
It was going to be a pillow for your head.
那本来是要当你的枕头的。

1233
00:49:01.220 --> 00:49:02.020
I guess so.
我想是吧。

1234
00:49:02.120 --> 00:49:04.620
A lot of people asked about the falling off the stool moment.
很多人问起从凳子上摔下来的那个镜头。

1235
00:49:04.800 --> 00:49:05.840
Was it scripted?
是剧本写的吗？

1236
00:49:05.960 --> 00:49:07.260
Did I actually do it?
是我真的摔了吗？

1237
00:49:07.380 --> 00:49:08.540
It was scripted.
是剧本写的。

1238
00:49:08.640 --> 00:49:09.980
I did actually do it.
我确实真的摔了。

1239
00:49:10.120 --> 00:49:15.300
But again, like being drunk, I was very nervous about falling off the stool and making it look
但就像演醉酒一样，我很担心摔下凳子时动作看起来

1240
00:49:15.300 --> 00:49:15.520
good.
不够自然。

1241
00:49:15.740 --> 00:49:21.120
So Greg Daniels, he got on the stool, and he showed me how he wanted me to fall.
所以格雷格·丹尼尔斯亲自坐上凳子，给我演示了他想要的摔法。

1242
00:49:21.280 --> 00:49:26.140
He said he wanted me to just keep looking at John and nodding, and then slowly slip off
他说他想让我一直看着约翰点头，然后慢慢地从

1243
00:49:26.140 --> 00:49:26.580
the stool.
凳子上滑下去。

1244
00:49:26.580 --> 00:49:28.220
And he's very large.
而且他块头很大。

1245
00:49:28.620 --> 00:49:28.840
He's very tall.
他非常高。

1246
00:49:28.840 --> 00:49:29.340
He's tall.
他很高。

1247
00:49:29.520 --> 00:49:30.600
He's like 6'2 or something.
他大概有6英尺2英寸（约1米88）左右吧。

1248
00:49:30.880 --> 00:49:32.320
And so he fell down.
于是他就摔下去了。

1249
00:49:32.380 --> 00:49:33.620
They had padding on the floor.
地板上铺了垫子。

1250
00:49:33.820 --> 00:49:36.280
So he and I were both falling on padding.
所以我和他都是摔在垫子上的。

1251
00:49:36.780 --> 00:49:42.840
But John Krasinski and I, we kept pretending like we didn't understand how I should fall
但约翰·卡拉辛斯基和我，我们一直假装不知道该怎么从

1252
00:49:42.840 --> 00:49:43.360
off the stool.
凳子上摔下来。

1253
00:49:43.360 --> 00:49:45.040
On purpose to mess with Greg?
故意去捉弄格雷格？

1254
00:49:45.280 --> 00:49:48.400
So that Greg would have to keep showing us.
这样格雷格就得一遍遍地演示给我们看。

1255
00:49:48.520 --> 00:49:49.340
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1256
00:49:49.440 --> 00:49:53.660
You were like, that's a moment where you were like real Jim and Pam, because you were pranking
你们当时就像是现实生活中的吉姆和帕姆，因为你们捉弄

1257
00:49:53.660 --> 00:49:55.980
Greg the way you would prank Dwight.
格雷格的方式就像你们捉弄德怀特一样。

1258
00:49:56.280 --> 00:49:57.520
A hundred percent.
百分之百是这样。

1259
00:49:57.700 --> 00:49:58.640
Does Greg know that?
格雷格知道吗？

1260
00:49:58.800 --> 00:49:59.180
He does.
他知道。

1261
00:49:59.620 --> 00:50:05.180
And then Greg told me later, I guess John and I told that story in an interview, and
后来格雷格告诉了我，我想是因为约翰和我曾在采访中讲过这个故事，然后

1262
00:50:05.180 --> 00:50:05.960
he confronted us.
他来找我们对质。

1263
00:50:06.080 --> 00:50:08.140
He was like, guys, you know, I really hurt my back doing that.
他说，伙计们，你们知道吗，我做那个动作真的伤到了背。

1264
00:50:08.140 --> 00:50:09.220
No, he did not.
不，他才没有。

1265
00:50:09.220 --> 00:50:11.940
So we were, then we felt so bad.
所以我们当时感觉特别内疚。

1266
00:50:12.800 --> 00:50:21.910
Oh my God, you guys, you, that was real life Jim Pam moment.
天哪，你们，那真是现实版的吉姆和帕姆时刻。

1267
00:50:22.050 --> 00:50:25.010
It was, it was, but I love doing that.
确实是，确实是，但我很喜欢那样做。

1268
00:50:25.230 --> 00:50:26.370
I love doing that stunt.
我很喜欢做那个特技。

1269
00:50:26.530 --> 00:50:28.110
I thought it ended up looking really good too.
我觉得最后呈现的效果也非常好。

1270
00:50:28.230 --> 00:50:28.990
I was proud of it.
我为它感到自豪。

1271
00:50:29.090 --> 00:50:30.170
I thought it looked fantastic.
我觉得看起来棒极了。

1272
00:50:30.350 --> 00:50:34.810
I thought that whole like part where you were nodding and then you were like, what?
我觉得你们点头然后说“什么？”的那整段戏，

1273
00:50:34.950 --> 00:50:35.550
And he was like, what?
他说“什么？”，

1274
00:50:35.630 --> 00:50:36.490
And then you start laughing.
然后你们就开始笑。

1275
00:50:36.730 --> 00:50:37.770
It was so perfect.
那真是太完美了。

1276
00:50:38.070 --> 00:50:39.070
It was so perfect.
那真是太完美了。

1277
00:50:39.070 --> 00:50:43.350
This brings us to the scene with Jim in the parking lot that we were talking about a little
这让我们想到了我们之前提到过的吉姆在停车场的那个场景，

1278
00:50:43.350 --> 00:50:43.910
bit earlier.
稍微提过一点。

1279
00:50:44.330 --> 00:50:48.090
A lot of people wanted to know what was Pam going to ask Jim.
很多人想知道帕姆当时到底想问吉姆什么。

1280
00:50:48.430 --> 00:50:51.010
She wanted to bring up so many things.
她想提的事情太多了。

1281
00:50:51.050 --> 00:50:51.630
So I think.
所以我想。

1282
00:50:51.830 --> 00:50:56.250
And it's, that's what stopped her because there were so many options going through her
这就是让她停下来的原因，因为那一刻她脑海里闪过了

1283
00:50:56.250 --> 00:50:57.050
head in that moment.
太多选择了。

1284
00:50:57.090 --> 00:51:03.370
And I had written out in my script all of these things that I could possibly say so that
我在剧本里写下了所有我可能要说的话，这样

1285
00:51:03.370 --> 00:51:08.110
I could in that moment rifle through them, but then not pick any of them.
我可以在那一刻快速浏览一遍，但最后什么都没选。

1286
00:51:08.110 --> 00:51:08.530
Right.
没错。

1287
00:51:09.090 --> 00:51:13.450
I think, I think it's that moment where you have so much to say and you're like, can
我觉得，我觉得那一刻就是你有太多话想说，然后你说“我能

1288
00:51:13.450 --> 00:51:14.410
I ask you a question?
问你个问题吗？”

1289
00:51:14.850 --> 00:51:19.610
And then it would just, the floodgates would have opened, but you saw the camera and it
然后话匣子就会彻底打开，但你看到了摄像机，它

1290
00:51:19.610 --> 00:51:22.330
gave you sort of this like check of like, I can't do this.
让你冷静了一下，意识到“我不能这么做”。

1291
00:51:22.450 --> 00:51:23.510
Not here, not now.
不是在这里，不是现在。

1292
00:51:23.650 --> 00:51:30.030
And I'm so glad that she didn't because those kind of drunken confessional conversations,
我很高兴她没说，因为那种酒后的坦白对话，

1293
00:51:30.030 --> 00:51:33.550
that wasn't going to lead to the right place.
并不会带来好的结果。

1294
00:51:34.210 --> 00:51:37.570
You know, I'm glad the camera was there for them in that moment.
你知道，我很高兴那一刻摄像机在那里。

1295
00:51:38.030 --> 00:51:42.330
Because I think what Pam was going to say, what I had written in my script was something
因为我觉得帕姆当时想说的，也就是我在剧本里写的，大概是

1296
00:51:42.330 --> 00:51:44.570
along the lines of, I love you.
类似于“我爱你”之类的话。

1297
00:51:44.890 --> 00:51:49.010
Well, I think the question was going to be, you know, do you think I should break up with
嗯，我觉得那个问题应该是，“你觉得我应该和

1298
00:51:49.010 --> 00:51:49.250
Roy?
罗伊分手吗？”

1299
00:51:49.470 --> 00:51:49.750
Yeah.
是的。

1300
00:51:49.970 --> 00:51:52.410
What do you, do you think I'm with the wrong person?
你觉得，你觉得我是不是跟错人在一起了？

1301
00:51:52.630 --> 00:51:52.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1302
00:51:53.050 --> 00:51:53.910
Those kind of leading questions.
那种引导性的问题。

1303
00:51:54.070 --> 00:51:55.870
Hoping that he'd say, you are, be with me.
希望他说，你是，和我在一起吧。

1304
00:51:55.870 --> 00:51:56.670
Yes, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1305
00:51:57.510 --> 00:51:58.850
So here's a crazy thing.
所以有件疯狂的事。

1306
00:51:58.930 --> 00:52:04.670
We mentioned earlier that our second season only had six episodes picked up, that this
我们之前提到过，第二季只预订了六集，而这

1307
00:52:04.670 --> 00:52:06.410
was the third episode that we shot.
是我们拍摄的第三集。

1308
00:52:06.670 --> 00:52:11.650
And we didn't know this was going to be the premiere of season two when we shot it.
我们拍的时候并不知道这会是第二季的首播集。

1309
00:52:11.730 --> 00:52:17.130
In fact, one of the ideas was that if we got canceled, it would be the season finale.
事实上，当时的想法之一是，如果我们被砍了，这就是季终集。

1310
00:52:17.130 --> 00:52:25.630
And so I said to Greg, I think just in case we get canceled, and this is the season finale,
所以我对格雷格说，我想以防我们被砍，如果这就是季终集的话，

1311
00:52:25.970 --> 00:52:32.730
I think we should film an alternate ending to this scene in the parking lot where Pam does
我觉得我们应该在停车场为这场戏拍一个备用结局，让帕姆

1312
00:52:32.730 --> 00:52:35.870
tell Jim how she feels and they kiss for real.
告诉吉姆她的感受，然后他们真的亲吻了。

1313
00:52:36.150 --> 00:52:41.530
Not the Chili's kiss, but the real kiss just so that we could air it and we don't leave
不是在Chili's的那种吻，而是真正的吻，这样我们就能播出，不会让

1314
00:52:41.530 --> 00:52:42.270
people hanging.
观众悬着心。

1315
00:52:43.430 --> 00:52:45.730
And Greg said, no.
格雷格说，不行。

1316
00:52:47.130 --> 00:52:48.150
He said, no.
他说，不行。

1317
00:52:48.410 --> 00:52:52.290
If they want to see what happens with Jim and Pam, they're just going to have to order
如果他们想看吉姆和帕姆后来怎么样了，他们就只能去订购

1318
00:52:52.290 --> 00:52:53.210
more episodes.
更多的剧集。

1319
00:52:53.670 --> 00:52:54.910
I don't want to give them a choice.
我不想给他们选择的机会。

1320
00:52:55.170 --> 00:52:55.930
There you go.
就是这样。

1321
00:52:56.070 --> 00:52:58.130
He was very protective of Jim and Pam, too.
他对吉姆和帕姆也非常保护。

1322
00:52:58.130 --> 00:52:58.430
He was.
确实如此。

1323
00:52:58.550 --> 00:53:00.950
And what went out in the world about that relationship.
以及关于那段关系向外界传达了什么。

1324
00:53:01.270 --> 00:53:04.970
But that shows you how much we thought we were going to be canceled.
但这说明我们当时有多觉得会被砍掉。

1325
00:53:05.230 --> 00:53:05.470
Yeah.
是啊。

1326
00:53:05.470 --> 00:53:06.110
All the time.
一直都是。

1327
00:53:06.290 --> 00:53:06.770
All the time.
一直都是。

1328
00:53:06.870 --> 00:53:11.030
That I was pitching ideas for how to wrap up the whole series.
我一直在提议如何给整部剧收尾。

1329
00:53:11.270 --> 00:53:11.790
Well, listen.
好吧，听着。

1330
00:53:11.790 --> 00:53:12.590
Just in case.
以防万一。

1331
00:53:12.850 --> 00:53:17.050
If you think that a normal show gets, well, at that time, networked,
如果你认为一部正常的剧集，嗯，在那个时候，电视网，

1332
00:53:17.050 --> 00:53:19.790
TV, you would get 22 episodes and we got six.
电视节目，你会得到22集，而我们只得到了6集。

1333
00:53:19.970 --> 00:53:23.290
It doesn't make you feel like anyone's really confident about what you're doing.
这让你觉得没人对你们在做的事情有信心。

1334
00:53:23.510 --> 00:53:26.490
Like, we didn't think NBC was like, oh, we got a winner here.
就像，我们不觉得NBC会觉得，哦，我们捡到宝了。

1335
00:53:26.810 --> 00:53:28.890
I have some deleted scenes cards.
我有一些删减片段的卡片。

1336
00:53:29.330 --> 00:53:30.170
Oh, tell them.
哦，告诉他们。

1337
00:53:30.310 --> 00:53:34.430
Well, one of the ones I really loved is that Toby does a talking head where he says he's
嗯，我非常喜欢的一段是托比做了一个采访，他说他

1338
00:53:34.430 --> 00:53:35.470
never won a Dundee.
从来没拿过邓迪奖。

1339
00:53:35.770 --> 00:53:36.470
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1340
00:53:36.770 --> 00:53:38.830
Michael refuses to give Toby a Dundee.
迈克尔拒绝给托比颁发邓迪奖。

1341
00:53:38.950 --> 00:53:40.110
He just leaves him out every year.
他每年都把他排除在外。

1342
00:53:40.110 --> 00:53:43.070
And now everyone in the office gets a Dundee but Toby.
现在办公室里每个人都拿过邓迪奖，就托比没有。

1343
00:53:43.290 --> 00:53:45.270
And I think, and Toby's like, I'm okay with that.
我觉得，托比当时说，我没关系。

1344
00:53:45.410 --> 00:53:46.390
I thought that was really funny.
我觉得那真的很有趣。

1345
00:53:46.550 --> 00:53:52.550
And then there's a great Dwight Angela scene at the copier where Dwight is really trying
还有一段很棒的德怀特和安吉拉在复印机旁的戏，德怀特真的在试图

1346
00:53:52.550 --> 00:53:55.970
